<title>BELGIUM: EU reviews Ahold/CSC joint buy of Store 2000.</title>
<headline>EU reviews Ahold/CSC joint buy of Store 2000.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Friday it was reviewing a deal under which Dutch retail food group Koninklijke Ahold NV and Central de Serveis Ciencies (CSC) will acquire joint control of Spanish food retail firm Store 2000.</p>
<p>It said the operation was submitted for clearance on October 30 under the merger regulation 4064/89. The Commission has about a month from that date to clear the deal or start a full probe.</p>
<p>The deal also involved Ahold's subsidiary in Spain, the Commission said in a statement. CSC is also a food retail firm in Catalunia and the Balearic Islands.</p>
</text>
